 "version": 1,
 "comment": "Deception conformance (sdk/rasp/README.md \"Deception\"). Written by hand from the contract; Shield360 Edge (cli/internal/edge) and every SDK run all of it. `config`: the signed config's `deception` value (a missing key means absent) and the block an SDK keeps, or null for none (deception off). `match`: each case's decoys (default: the top-level `decoys`, read through the same config rules) and a request target in origin form (path and optional query); `expect` is the decoy it hits, or null. The path (before the first `?`) is percent-decoded once (every %XX, %2F included; an invalid escape matches nothing), compared byte for byte (UTF-8) and case-sensitively, never cleaned of dot segments or doubled slashes, and matches a decoy that it equals or that it is under on a segment boundary (decoy + \"/\"). The first matching decoy in config order wins.",
